        "design_plan": false
      },
      "time": "~20s",
      "narrative": "Once agents are running, the question is simple: are they doing the job the right way? \n\nLet’s take a close up look at agent performance, in Foundry. \n",
      "demo_actions": "Open the Foundry post-deployment view and frame this chapter as performance inspection.",
      "screenshot": ".cutready/screenshots/20260630_073751_057_2.jpg"
    },
    {
      "locked": false,
      "locks": {
        "time": false,
        "narrative": false,
        "demo_actions": false,
        "screenshot": false,
        "visual": false,
        "design_plan": false
      },
      "time": "~30s",
      "narrative": "Start with tracing. I want to see the path through the evidence — which records the agent read, and every step it took before it made a call. \n\nThat turns each run from a black box into something the team can actually inspect. \n",
      "demo_actions": "Open trace details for an invoice-review run. Show the sequence of evidence access and reasoning steps.",
      "screenshot": ".cutready/screenshots/20260630_073811_074_6.jpg"
    },
    {
