      },
      "time": "~30s",
      "narrative": "Next, I turn to my rubrics. And this is the magic. Rubrics operate just like how a teacher uses a rubric to guide for grading for their students, rubrics guide the agent's work: is it reasoning correctly over the contract terms, using the right evidence, producing a clear and defensible recommendation? \n\nThe system can even generate that rubric from the agent itself, so the team isn't inventing evaluation criteria from a blank page. \n",
      "demo_actions": "Open Foundry rubric evaluators. Show criteria tied to contract reasoning, evidence use, and recommendation quality.",
      "screenshot": ".cutready/screenshots/20260630_073849_749_10.jpg"
    },
    {
      "locked": false,
      "locks": {
        "time": false,
        "narrative": false,
        "demo_actions": false,
        "screenshot": false,
        "visual": false,
        "design_plan": false
      },
      "time": "~30s",
      "narrative": "With the rubric set, we run evaluations against it. \n\nNow we can see exactly where the agent is strong and where it still misses — our performance is measured, not anecdotal. \n",
      "demo_actions": "Run or review evaluation results. Show scores, failures, and examples.",
      "screenshot": ".cutready/screenshots/20260630_073922_018_14.jpg"
    },
    {
